      "text": "1. Calculate the sum of the digits of the first number: $2+9=11$. Find the first number with this property:  The tens place should be 2, and the ones digit should be 9 (having the smallest number)\n\n2. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $2+10+8=11$. Find the second number with this property: The tens place should be $10$, hence the number is $19, having the smallest number ending to have this property.\n\n3. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $10+9+8=11$. Find the third number with this property: The tens place should be $9$, hence the number is $189, having the smallest number ending to have this property.\n\n4. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $9+8+10=17 \\neq 11$. hence keep $189$ which is also the 3rd number.\n\n5. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $8+9+10=27 \\neq 11$. hence keep $189$ which is also the 3rd number.\n\n6. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $7+8+9=24 \\neq 11$. hence keep $189$ which is also the 3rd number.\n\n7. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $6+7+8=21 \\neq 11$. hence keep $189$ which is also the 3rd number.\n\n8. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $5+6+7=18 \\neq 11$. hence keep $189$ which is also the 3rd number.\n\n9. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $4+5+6=15 \\neq 11$. hence keep $189$ which is also the 3rd number.\n\n10. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $3+4+5=12 \\neq 11$. hence keep $189$ which is also the 3rd number.\n\n11. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $2+3+4=9 \\neq 11$. hence keep $189$ which is also the 3rd number.\n\n11. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $11=12 \\neq 11$. hence keep $189$ which is also the 3rd number.\n\n12. Calculate the sum of the digits of the next number: $22=22 \\neq 11$. hence $\\boxed{189}$",
